<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alivardi Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1671–1756</span> · Also known as Allahverdi Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alivardi Khan was Nawab of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Orissa</a> from 1740 to 1756, having seized power by defeating Sarfaraz Khan at Giria. Much of his reign was spent fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> raids, ended by a treaty of 1751 that ceded Orissa's revenues. He was succeeded by his grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siraj-ud-daulah">Siraj ud-Daulah</a>, defeated at Plassey in 1757.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alivardi-khan.jpg" alt="Alivardi Khan" width="320" height="463" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Darbar_of_Alivardi_Khan_at_Murshidabad%27s_Court_MET_DP-19635-001_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
